# The ChromaDB knowledge base is committed so a fresh clone and the Docker
# image have working RAG with no setup step. ChromaDB rewrites these files
# whenever the DB is opened, so they show as modified after any test run even
# when the contents are identical.
#
# Marking them binary keeps that churn out of diffs and stops git attempting a
# textual merge on a 9.8MB SQLite file.
#
# CAUTION: `git checkout -- backend/data/chroma_db` discards *real* ingest
# results as readily as it discards open-on-read churn, and the two are
# indistinguishable in `git status`. Always confirm with
# `python -m backend.embeddings.rebuild_kb --verify` afterwards; if a
# collection comes back EMPTY or THIN, re-run the ingest.
backend/data/chroma_db/** binary -diff -merge

# Committed reference documents and model checkpoints — never text-merge.
*.pdf   binary -diff
*.pkl   binary -diff
*.fts   binary -diff
